	•	Study Design: Retrospective Cohort
	•	AI Model Architecture: Random Forest
	•	Algorithm Name: Random Survival Forests (RSF); temporal decomposition parametric survival model
	•	Input Variables (Data Modality): Tabular (EMR/Clinical data), Donor metrics
	•	Comparator / Standard of Care: None
	•	Validation Method: Not Reported
	•	Explainability / Interpretability Used: No
	•	Feature Selection Method: Automated (e.g., LASSO, Stepwise)
	•	Hyperparameter Tuning Reported: No
	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The study used “two complimentary time-related analyses,” including a “random survival forests method” and a temporal decomposition model. RSF was used to determine “importance of mortality risk factors and their interactions.” Inputs were recipient and donor tabular variables from SRTR. The paper does not frame this against a human or guideline comparator. Variable screening in the sex-focused parametric models used “machine learning variable selection,” which is best categorized as automated. Explicit hyperparameter tuning was not reported.

