	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: The primary endpoint was “all-cause mortality assessed as time from heart transplantation to death or end of follow-up,” so the closest restricted category is Other. The study focused on hazard phases, variable importance, and interactions rather than reporting AUC, accuracy, sensitivity, specificity, PPV, NPV, or F1-score. Figure 1 showed 1-month survival 96%, 1-year survival 89%, and 12-year survival 50%, but these are cohort survival estimates rather than model discrimination metrics. Calibration and DCA were not reported.

